/**
 * @defgroup FtroGeo FtroGeo — STAR FTPC Readout Barrel Geometry
 * @ingroup StarVMCGeometry
 * @brief AGML geometry definition for the STAR Forward TPC readout barrel.
 * @details
 * The FTPC Readout (FTRO) module defines the mechanical and electronic
 * structures mounted on the outer (downstream) face of each Forward TPC disk.
 * Two identical readout barrels are placed at
 *   @f$ z = \pm(150 + 119 + 40) = \pm309 @f$ cm from the interaction point
 * (the −z instance is rotated 180° about the y-axis).
 *
 * Each barrel (@c FTMO) is a hollow annular cylinder (Rin = 15 cm,
 * Rout = 30 cm, length = 80 cm, filled with Air) divided into five azimuthal
 * sectors (@c FTCD).  Within each sector:
 *   - One aluminium I-beam strut (@c FSMO: flanges @c FSTL × 2 + web @c FSTC
 *     with 5 lightening holes @c FSHL).
 *   - One aluminium cover plank (@c FTPL) over the strut.
 *   - Two outer G10 PCB panels (@c FTPO) at radius 22 cm, one on each side of
 *     the sector centre.
 *   - Two inner G10 PCB panels (@c FTPI) at radius 20 cm.
 *   - One aluminium protective shell sector (@c FTSH, TUBS shape).
 * The barrel also carries an outer flange (@c FTOF, with 15 evenly spaced
 * holes @c FTOH at R = 26 cm), an inner flange (@c FTIF), and a rim ring
 * (@c FTRM).
 *
 * Key global parameters (structure @c FTRG):
 *   - N = 5 sectors
 *   - ftpcZ = 150 cm, ftpcLen = 119 cm, length = 80 cm
 *   - Rin = 15 cm, Rout = 30 cm
 *   - strutLen = 50 cm, strutHgt = 6.5 cm
 *   - ftpoR = 22 cm (outer PCB), ftpiR = 20 cm (inner PCB)
 *   - G10 (PCBs): inline mixture, density 1.7 g/cm³ (Si, O, C, H)
 * @{
 */

/**
 * @defgroup FtroGeo_v1 FtroGeo — FTPC readout barrel (single version)
 * @ingroup FtroGeo
 * @brief Module @c FTROGEO: the FTPC readout barrel geometry (Potekhin, 2004).
 * @details
 * Only one module version exists for detector FTRO.  The @c FTRG structure
 * (Version=1) fully characterises the geometry; no sub-version selector is
 * present.  The G10 mixture is defined inline within the module.
 *
 * Volume hierarchy:
 *   @c CAVE → @c FTMO → @c FTCM → @c FTCD (DIVISION, 5 sectors) →
 *   { @c FSMO (@c FSTL × 2, @c FSTC → @c FSHL × 5),
 *     @c FTPL, @c FTPO × 2, @c FTPI × 2, @c FTSH }
 *   and @c FTMO → { @c FTOF → @c FTOH × 15, @c FTIF, @c FTRM }.
 *
 * Activated by setups @c FTROon and @c FTRO01.
 */

/**
 * @}
 */
